Z||000000||bilbo||06-30-2001||02:30 PM||||Started on the exhaust manifolds,removed the Y pipe but could these manifolds be any harder to get off...I THINK NOT!!!! I've stripped just about all but two bolts any advice on how I could get a better grip on these things would be greatly appreciated.I've soaked with penetrating oil but they don't want to budge!!!I'm hoping someone has an idea to help me out before I set the car ablaze!!!! Any special tools or gadgets I can use to make it easier??!!!THanks Guy's!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||06-30-2001||08:50 PM||||ablaze is not too far off. You can use a welding torch to heat them up - just dont melt the heads off !!! keep fire extinguishers handy !!!! heat them, then knock them on the head with a hammer. If that dont work, just keep at it you have just started doing the very worst repair that you will have to do.||||reg||1
